# Files the Vercel CLI should not upload.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists, Vercel uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore for
# `vercel deploy` uploads, so every exclusion that matters has to be repeated
# here -- secrets included. Git-based deploys are unaffected (Vercel clones the
# repo), so this only shrinks CLI uploads.
#
# Why: `vercel --prod` uploads each file as its own request. This project was
# sending 533 files / 18 MB, and roughly 270 files of that are documentation and
# screenshots the build never reads. On a slow or unstable connection the
# uploader gives up with "fetch failed" / "AbortError: This operation was
# aborted". Dropping them roughly halves the payload.

# --- secrets and local state (must stay listed) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel
node_modules
.git

# --- build output, regenerated every deploy ---
dist
.output
.tanstack
src/generated/prisma
*.log

# --- backups written by scripts/optimize-images.mjs ---
public-original

# --- AI assistant skill libraries: 213 files of Prisma docs, never built ---
.agents
.claude
.windsurf
skills-lock.json
AGENTS.md

# --- development screenshots: 7.8 MB, larger than the entire public/ folder ---
screenshots
attachments
docs

# --- project documentation ---
CHANGES-ROUND-2.md
FIXES-ROUND-3.md
MERGE-NOTES.md
DEPLOY-VERCEL.md
DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md

# Kept on purpose, because the build genuinely needs them:
#   public/            static assets, icons, manifest, sw.js
#   scripts/           with-app-env.mjs, grok-pwa-plugin.mjs, install-page.html
#   migrations/        read by prisma.config.ts and vite.config.ts
#   prisma/            schema + seed
#   src/ server/       the app itself
